      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: optional info lines (IP, uptime, OS, location) on the name tag",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nThe name tag can now show live machine facts under the name: IP address, uptime, macOS version, and the fleet-file `location`. All four are individual checkboxes in Settings → Layers, off by default — an unconfigured tag renders exactly as before.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nOn a wall of Jump Desktop windows the tag tells you *which* Mac you're on, but the facts you reach for next (IP, uptime) live one menu click away, per machine. Putting selected fields on the glass is the one habit [BGInfo](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/bginfo) users can't replicate here yet — its ecosystem is still almost entirely [\"show hostname/IP on every machine\" deployment content](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yQh2CDq2qsg), and the Mac-side alternatives on [AlternativeTo's BGInfo page](https://alternativeto.net/software/bginfo/?platform=mac) are stale or repaint the wallpaper. Nameplate already samples everything needed in `SystemInfo`; this just renders it.\n\n## Demo\n\nSimulated demo:\n\n![demo](https://files.catbox.moe/dm3f0d.gif)\n\n## Changes\n\n- Formatting lives in `NameplateCore` (`InfoLine.swift`: field enum + pure formatter with test vectors); the app layer only samples and publishes. Keeps the core AppKit-free per the parity contract, so the Windows/Linux ports can reuse the field set later.\n- Sampling follows the `RemoteViewMonitor` discipline: a 60 s tolerance timer that only runs while at least one field is enabled. Empty selection means no timer and byte-for-byte today's pill.\n- Multiline tags switch from `Capsule` to a fixed-radius rounded rectangle so the first and last lines don't ride the curved edge; single-line tags keep the capsule.\n\n## Testing\n\n`swift build` and `swift test` pass (32 tests, including new `InfoLineTests` formatter vectors: IP with interface, uptime day/hour collapsing, OS version, empty-field omission).\n",
